tion\r\n\t\t\t\tThe [param draw_flags] indicates if the texture attachments of the framebuffer should get cleared or ignored. Only one of both flags can be used for each individual attachment. Ignoring an attachment means that any contents that existed before the draw list will be completely discarded. If you don't specify anything, the contents may be kept, which can reduce performance.\r\n```\r\n\r\nAs far as I understand it works as follows:\r\n1. If no flags, the graph is responsible for figuring out if a load is needed. For discardable textures, it can automatically fall back to ignore if the texture hasn't been used this frame. For non-discardable textures, you will end up loading\r\n2. If ignore, the graph will ignore\r\n3. if clear, the graph will clear","created_at":"2024-11-18T19:23:46Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T19:30:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98670#discussion_r1847131265","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98670","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1847131265"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98670#discussion_r1847131265"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98670"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1847131265/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":241,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":35,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1847179521","pull_request_review_id":2443585217,"id":1847179521,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5uGbkB","diff_hunk":"@@ -1084,7 +1084,7 @@ void RenderForwardMobile::_render_scene(RenderDataRD *p_render_data, const Color\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n \n-\t\tRD::DrawListID draw_list = RD::get_singleton()->draw_list_begin(framebuffer, load_color ? RD::INITIAL_ACTION_LOAD : RD::INITIAL_ACTION_CLEAR, RD::FINAL_ACTION_STORE, RD::INITIAL_ACTION_CLEAR, RD::FINAL_ACTION_STORE, c, 0.0, 0, Rect2(), breadcrumb);\n+\t\tRD::DrawListID draw_list = RD::get_singleton()->draw_list_begin(framebuffer, RD::DRAW_CLEAR_ALL, c, 0.0f, 0, Rect2(), breadcrumb);","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_mobile/render_forward_mobile.cpp","commit_id":"6d5ac8f7ef4a3ddaf50720ab473b9dffece21674","original_commit_id":"af068d7a192c95859702945ed6b1ff4d5be1b7fd","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I would expect this to produce an error. You are saying that all the color buffers should be cleared, but then you provide no colors in the color array. If a clear is requested, but no clear color is specified, we should throw an error. ","created_at":"2024-11-18T20:00:36Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T20:00:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98670#discussion_r1847179521","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/986